+## Request 21: Duplicate Customer Merging (COMPLETED)
+
+### What was done
+- Added mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId) to src/customers.js:
+  - Merges two customers: removes fromId customer and reassigns its invoices to intoId
+  - Returns ok({ customers, invoices }) with merged arrays
+  - Normalizes both customer IDs before processing
+  - Never mutates input arrays
+  - Validates both customers exist and are different
+- Added SAME_CUSTOMER error code to src/errors.js
+- Created test/merge-customers.test.js with 16 comprehensive test cases covering:
+  - Successful merge of invoices from one customer to another
+  - Same customer rejection (SAME_CUSTOMER)
+  - Unknown from customer rejection
+  - Unknown into customer rejection
+  - Normalized ID handling (case-insensitive, whitespace-trimmed)
+  - Non-mutation of input arrays
+  - Empty invoices array
+  - Multiple invoices from from-customer
+  - Preservation of other customers' invoices
+  - Draft invoices merge
+  - Partially paid invoices with payments preserved
+  - Customer properties preservation
+  - Null arrays handling
+  - Order preservation (customers and invoices)
+  - Case-insensitive ID matching
+- All 295 tests passing (16 new merge + 33 currency + 21 CSV + 10 late fee + 15 VAT + 16 overdue + 184 existing)
+
+### Design
+- fromId customer is completely removed from customers array
+- All invoices with fromId are reassigned to intoId
+- Other customers and their invoices unaffected
+- Invoice payments and metadata preserved during merge
+- ID normalization ensures case-insensitive matching
+- Non-mutating: returns new arrays
+
+### Use Cases
+- Consolidate duplicate customer records
+- Merge accounts that were accidentally split
+- Handle company name changes or restructuring
+- Clean up after customer data imports
+
 ## Next Steps
 - Available for future invoice features (persistence, API endpoints, etc.)
